SOGo on FenrirOS
================

Nothing runs and nothing is configured by default. SOGo runs as _sogo
(home /var/lib/sogo); its configuration is /etc/sogo/sogo.conf (an
OpenStep property list; start from /etc/sogo/sogo.conf.sample, upstream's
all-commented example, and the SOGo Installation Guide).

1. memcached: dinitctl enable memcached (it listens on 127.0.0.1:11211;
   SOGoMemcachedHost = "127.0.0.1";).
2. Database (PostgreSQL or MariaDB). PostgreSQL:
     createuser -P sogo ; createdb -O sogo sogo
   then in sogo.conf (SOGo creates its tables itself):
     SOGoProfileURL = "postgresql://sogo:<password>@localhost:5432/sogo/sogo_user_profile";
     OCSFolderInfoURL = "postgresql://sogo:<password>@localhost:5432/sogo/sogo_folder_info";
     OCSSessionsFolderURL = "postgresql://sogo:<password>@localhost:5432/sogo/sogo_sessions_folder";
   (MariaDB: mysql://...; see /usr/share/doc/sogo/mysql-utf8mb4.sql.)
3. Users: SOGoUserSources (LDAP or an SQL view), and mail: SOGoIMAPServer,
   SOGoSMTPServer, SOGoSieveServer, SOGoMailDomain. Keep the file private:
     cp /etc/sogo/sogo.conf.sample /etc/sogo/sogo.conf
     chown root:_sogo /etc/sogo/sogo.conf ; chmod 640 /etc/sogo/sogo.conf
4. The service's command line (127.0.0.1:20000, 3 workers, log in
   /var/log/sogo) is /etc/dinit.d/sogo. Then: dinitctl enable sogo
5. Web server: /usr/share/doc/sogo/nginx-sogo.conf (nginx proxies to
   sogod and serves the web resources); dinitctl enable nginx.
6. Scheduled jobs (session expiry, e-mail alarms, vacation messages,
   backups) are examples in /usr/share/doc/sogo/sogo.cron: copy the lines
   you want to /etc/cron.d/sogo (user _sogo, programs in /usr/bin) and
   dinitctl enable crond. Log rotation example: /usr/share/doc/sogo/logrotate.
7. Two-factor authentication: SOGoTOTPEnabled = YES; in sogo.conf.
8. ActiveSync (phones) is the separate package sogo-activesync; upstream
   says production use needs a licence from Microsoft
   (/usr/share/doc/sogo/README.ActiveSync).

sogo-tool (in /usr/bin) manages users, backups and restores; run it as
_sogo: su -s /bin/sh _sogo -c 'sogo-tool ...'.
